      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "That is the kind of problem I had last month. I have an avatar at like 68k polygons, was rated medium. Then I went to add a nice hoodie and the polygons went above 70k and thus poor.\n\nA new defined area between 70k and 100K (or a bit less) polygons would be pretty neat here to not kick the overall rating all the way to the bottom when it happens.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-09T11:25:49.414Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is my Request to up the Poly Limits for Poor rated to around 100k on PC and 32k on Quest.\nPolygons themselves don't normally affect Performance that much, and it makes little sense to make them so low. \nThis isn't changing the Poly Limit on Medium or Good. It's adding a little bit of a barrier between medium and poor avatars and bringing about less VERY Poor Avatars. Often I've had the time where I'd be like 3 or 4k over the Poly Limit due to props I have togglable. I fell a change like this would make optimizations a bit better for people.",
